// the user's odd8 proof: unlabeled cases, blank lines inside a case, "in all exhaustive cases"
wts x is odd implies 8 divides x^2 - 1

assume x is odd. then exists k in integers such that x = 2k + 1. then
$
x^2 - 1 = (2k + 1)^2 - 1 = (4k^2 + 4k + 1) - 1 = 4k^2 + 4k
$

case k is odd. then exists l in integers st k = 2l + 1. then
$4k^2 + 4k = 4(2l+1)^2 + 4(2l+1) = 4(4l^2 + 4l + 1) + 4(2l+1) = 8(2l^2+2l) + 8 + 8l = 8 (2l^2+3l+1)$

Observe (2l^2+3l+1) in integers, so by definition of divisibility, 8 | (x^2 - 1).

case k is even. then exists l in integers st k = 2l. then 4k^2 + 4k = 4 * 4l^2 + 8l = 8 (2l^2+l).

Observe (2l^2+l) in integers, so by definition of divisibility 8 | (x^2 - 1).

In all exhaustive cases, 8 | (x^2 - 1), and thus x is odd implies 8 | (x^2 - 1).

qed
